{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>Will You destroy the whole city for five?</b> Inform me whether there is a fixed number before You — fewer than ten per large city — below which there will be no interceding congregation, and accordingly You would destroy the city that is fifth-most culpable, on account of there being no interceding congregation for it." "<b>And He said, I will not destroy.</b> The fifth."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {0 "The phrase החמישית היותר חייבת, literally 'the fifth most guilty,' is understood as Sforno's way of ranking cities by culpability; 'fifth-most culpable' renders it hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:30:42.196461363Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}